// [word, part of speech, definition, correct use, correct use, incorrect use].
// The impostor keeps the same part of speech but contradicts the stated sense;
// learners must judge meaning rather than spot a grammatical category change.
// Keep order stable: these rows are part of the dated daily-content contract.
